#X text 385 334 The [pluck.m~] is the MERDA version of [pluck~]., f 27;
#X text 22 24 The ELSE library has the [pluck~] object \, which implements a Karplus Strong Algorithm. By default \, it uses an internal white noise generator as an excitation signal and can be triggered by impulses. A frequency value determines the delay period and the excitation signal gets automatically enveloped to that size. The feedback value is given as a decay time in ms (t60). Internally \, it has a 1st order lowpass filter in the feedback loop just like [lop3~]. You can also configure the object to have arbitrary noise inputs. See its help file for more details., f 74;
